  "id": "automatic-speech",
  "term": "automatic speech",
  "definition": "In this historical source, automatic speech means spontaneous, self-directed talking that runs on by itself, like soliloquising or prattling. It is described as speech produced with little active attention to the outside world, as in simple mania.",
